WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.250
The New Forest, in Hampshire, became
a royal hunting forest in about 1079.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.870
Its ancient oaks, beech and holly support
an extraordinary range of wildlife.

3
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.230
Each summer, the oaks and beeches
spread a full green canopy.

4
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.350
Each autumn, they drop every leaf.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.770
Why would a tree throw away
every leaf it has grown?

6
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.310
For a new colour?

7
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.600
Hungry insects?

8
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.450
In this mission, you'll
explore how climate,

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.050
soil, plants and animals fit
together in a deciduous wood.

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.930
Then you'll find out how plants and
animals adapt to the changing seasons.

11
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain why oak
and beech go bare every autumn.
